<title>PAKISTAN: Bank of America to finance Pakistan wheat imports.</title>
<headline>Bank of America to finance Pakistan wheat imports.</headline>
<dateline>KARACHI, Pakistan 1996-10-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Bank of America will provide $125 million financing to two nationalised Pakistani banks for wheat imports, Nauman Dar, the bank's country credit and marketing manager said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>The financing facility for three years would be provided to the National Bank of Pakistan and Habib Bank Ltd, enabling them to issue import letters of credit of up to $125 million on behalf of the Pakistan government in favour of U.S. suppliers.</p>
<p>Dar said U.S. exporters would be paid at sight by the bank. Shipment under this facility was likely to take place within 12 months, he added.</p>
<p>Bank of America is a unit of BankAmerica Corp.</p>
<p>-- Ibrahim Khan 9221-5685192</p>
</text>
